<title>USA: Blyth Industries acquisition cleared.</title>
<headline>Blyth Industries acquisition cleared.</headline>
<dateline>GREENWICH, Conn. 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blyth Industries Inc said Tuesday the U.S. Federal Trade Commission has granted early termination of the waiting period under the Hart-Scott-Rodino Antitrust Improvements Act with respect to the proposed acquisition of Endar Corp.</p>
<p>This clears the way for Blyth to proceed with its previously announced plan to purchase the privately-held manufacturer and marketer of environmental home fragrance products and accessories.</p>
<p>Chief executive Robert B. Goergen said he expects the transaction will close by early June, subject to the satisfaction of certain other conditions.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
